// Built-in Regex type. The automata live in stdlib/regex/regex.xr; the class
// is only the handle, and it exists as a native class because the literal
// syntax /pat/flags lowers to XI_REGEX_COMPILE with its result type pinned to
// type_regex (src/ir/xi_lower_expr.c:11349).
//
// `prog` is the compiled program image, produced and memoised by regex.xr. It
// is a plain GC-visible field rather than a native body because
// XrNativeBodyDesc has no trace callback, so a native body cannot hold an
// Xray value without the collector losing it. It starts empty and regex.xr
// fills it by pushing: a class-typed parameter is a read capability, so the
// field itself cannot be assigned from there, but its elements can.
class Regex {
    pattern: string
    flags: i64
    prog: Array<i64>
}
